# Feature implementation

Use this for a feature or a change that crosses a system boundary. A one-line fix with an obvious site does not need the full pass.

## Understand

Read Docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md. Default docs path: mother section → one matching child; read Docs/README.md only when authority or docs process is unclear. Read matching Docs/DECISIONS/ and any in-progress feature spec before proposing design. Read Docs/GDD.md when the task affects gameplay. Read Docs/TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md when it affects a boundary. Read the feature spec in Docs/FEATURE_SPECS/ when that feature has one. Inspect the existing implementation before proposing a new type. Do not reopen an accepted decision without new facts.

## Plan

Name the files, the owner each change extends, the risks, and the tests. Do this before editing.

A large feature, or a missing decision that would change the result, stops here. This is the planning stage. Post the implementation plan and the acceptance criteria. Do not edit code, scenes, or assets until the user agrees.

## Implement

Once the plan is agreed, implement one coherent part at a time. Stay inside the current `ROADMAP.md` gate. Do not start the next gate until that gate's exit criteria are met. Extend the owner in Docs/TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md. Follow .cursor/rules/. When the task is UI, follow the UI rule in .cursor/rules/ if one exists. Do not invent a gameplay rule or edit an unrelated system.

A persistence, recovery, or concurrent-session feature waits until the normal success path has been played and its result has survived a reload. Do not debug the happy path and the failure path in the same change.

## Verify

Follow Docs/TEST_STRATEGY.md. Run the tests that cover the change when they can be run. Name anything that still needs the Unity Editor. Play Mode counts only if it was entered.

## Report

State what changed, the test results, any deviation from the plan, and what is still unverified.

## Update

Change Docs/GDD.md, Docs/TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md, Docs/ROADMAP.md, Docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md, or a feature spec only when this change altered a rule, a boundary, a requirement, or the current state. A new architectural decision goes in Docs/DECISIONS/ and into Docs/TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md. Do not write a document that only repeats the report.
